1
00:00:05,455 --> 00:00:07,304
A lamp burns through the night.

2
00:00:07,384 --> 00:00:11,625
In the last watch, its flame is
not the flame of the first watch.

3
00:00:11,705 --> 00:00:14,519
The oil is different. The wick is shorter.

4
00:00:14,599 --> 00:00:19,170
And yet there was never a moment when
one flame stopped and another began.

5
00:00:19,993 --> 00:00:23,867
Now light a second lamp from
the first. Nothing passes over.

6
00:00:23,946 --> 00:00:27,141
No small piece of the
first flame jumps across.

7
00:00:27,221 --> 00:00:31,027
And yet the second flame is
not unconnected with the first.

8
00:00:31,107 --> 00:00:32,322
It was lit from it.

9
00:00:33,138 --> 00:00:37,216
This is the oldest image the
Buddhist tradition has for rebirth.

10
00:00:37,296 --> 00:00:40,794
To see why it is the right one,
we have to start with a puzzle.

11
00:00:41,601 --> 00:00:45,570
Every Buddhist tradition
teaches that actions bear fruit,

12
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:48,491
and that one life conditions the next.

13
00:00:48,571 --> 00:00:54,571
Every Buddhist tradition also teaches that
there is no self. No soul. No inner owner.

14
00:00:54,794 --> 00:00:58,971
Nothing that stays the same
beneath the changing body and mind.

15
00:00:59,786 --> 00:01:03,185
Put side by side, these can
look like a contradiction.

16
00:01:03,265 --> 00:01:06,391
If there is no one who
dies, who is reborn?

17
00:01:06,471 --> 00:01:10,481
If nothing passes over, in what
sense is the next life mine?

18
00:01:10,561 --> 00:01:13,203
And if it is not mine, why should I care?

19
00:01:14,022 --> 00:01:16,524
The contradiction is only apparent.

20
00:01:16,604 --> 00:01:20,994
It rests on one assumption:
that continuity needs a carrier.

21
00:01:21,074 --> 00:01:26,116
Remove that assumption, and rebirth is no
harder to make sense of than waking up in

22
00:01:26,196 --> 00:01:27,396
the morning.

23
00:01:27,933 --> 00:01:30,312
Most of us picture rebirth like this.

24
00:01:30,392 --> 00:01:34,823
Inside each person is a
someone, a soul or a spark.

25
00:01:34,903 --> 00:01:36,508
The body is its house.

26
00:01:36,588 --> 00:01:39,864
At death the house falls,
and the someone moves out,

27
00:01:39,944 --> 00:01:43,142
travels, and moves into a new house.

28
00:01:43,958 --> 00:01:46,242
The skeptic uses the same picture.

29
00:01:46,322 --> 00:01:49,449
There is no someone
inside, the skeptic says.

30
00:01:49,529 --> 00:01:51,460
The mind is what the brain does.

31
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:54,938
When the brain stops,
nothing is left to move out.

32
00:01:55,018 --> 00:01:59,164
The believer and the skeptic agree
that rebirth would need a traveler.

33
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:01,858
They disagree only about
whether there is one.

34
00:02:02,682 --> 00:02:04,301
But look at an ordinary day.

35
00:02:04,381 --> 00:02:07,181
You fall asleep at night
and wake in the morning.

36
00:02:07,261 --> 00:02:10,754
You take it for granted that
the same someone slept and woke.

37
00:02:10,834 --> 00:02:14,450
Yet in deep sleep, nothing
at all is experienced.

38
00:02:14,530 --> 00:02:16,855
No witness keeps watch through the gap.

39
00:02:16,935 --> 00:02:20,822
The body of ten years ago has
been replaced, cell by cell.

40
00:02:20,902 --> 00:02:23,897
Its moods and plans are
not the ones it has now.

41
00:02:24,705 --> 00:02:29,462
And still, the person who wakes
is, by every ordinary standard,

42
00:02:29,542 --> 00:02:34,421
the person who fell asleep. They keep
their promises. They pay their debts.

43
00:02:34,501 --> 00:02:36,246
They recognize their friends.

44
00:02:37,069 --> 00:02:41,866
So the question of rebirth is only the
sharpest form of a question that comes

45
00:02:41,946 --> 00:02:46,377
every morning. If continuity
within a life needs no traveler,

46
00:02:46,457 --> 00:02:49,996
continuity between lives
does not need one either.

47
00:02:50,855 --> 00:02:54,742
From the start, the Buddha taught
against two opposite views.

48
00:02:54,822 --> 00:02:59,348
The first is eternalism: a
self that persists unchanged,

49
00:02:59,428 --> 00:03:03,791
so that the same one who acted in
a past life now meets the result.

50
00:03:03,871 --> 00:03:08,424
The second is annihilationism: a
self that is wiped out at death,

51
00:03:08,504 --> 00:03:12,029
or a later being who has nothing
to do with the earlier one.

52
00:03:12,850 --> 00:03:18,327
The tradition treats annihilationism as
the shadow of eternalism, not its cure.

53
00:03:18,407 --> 00:03:23,287
To say a self is destroyed, you must
first assume there was a self to destroy.

54
00:03:23,367 --> 00:03:27,512
And to say the later life has nothing
to do with the earlier ignores the plain

55
00:03:27,592 --> 00:03:29,224
dependence between them.

56
00:03:29,304 --> 00:03:33,277
The rice that grows from a seed
has something to do with the seed.

57
00:03:34,094 --> 00:03:37,873
Between these two, the Buddha
taught dependent arising.

58
00:03:37,953 --> 00:03:41,650
This being, that comes to
be. Life conditions life.

59
00:03:41,730 --> 00:03:43,349
Deed conditions fruit.

60
00:03:43,429 --> 00:03:45,726
Nothing carries the one into the other.

61
00:03:45,806 --> 00:03:47,538
And nothing cuts them apart.

62
00:03:48,354 --> 00:03:53,573
The Middle Way of Nāgārjuna tests every
candidate for a carrier in the same way.

63
00:03:53,653 --> 00:03:56,916
It asks: if this thing
had a nature of its own,

64
00:03:56,996 --> 00:04:00,059
where would that nature
be found? Then it looks.

65
00:04:00,886 --> 00:04:05,073
The Sanskrit word for that
nature is svabhāva, own nature.

66
00:04:05,153 --> 00:04:09,529
Something with own nature would be
what it is from its own side. Not made.

67
00:04:09,609 --> 00:04:12,604
Not depending on anything
else. Not changing.

68
00:04:13,405 --> 00:04:16,246
A soul that never changes could not learn,

69
00:04:16,326 --> 00:04:18,542
or suffer, or be freed.

70
00:04:18,622 --> 00:04:23,257
A stream of subtle consciousness
is either the same at every moment,

71
00:04:23,337 --> 00:04:26,980
and then it does not flow,
or different at every moment,

72
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:29,765
and then it is not one
thing carrying anything.

73
00:04:29,845 --> 00:04:33,094
A store of seeds either
holds them unchanged,

74
00:04:33,174 --> 00:04:36,101
and then they never ripen,
or changes with them,

75
00:04:36,190 --> 00:04:38,764
and then it is one more changing process.

76
00:04:39,569 --> 00:04:44,584
Each candidate, examined, turns out
to be one more dependent appearance.

77
00:04:44,664 --> 00:04:46,513
It needs a carrier of its own.

78
00:04:46,593 --> 00:04:48,474
And so no carrier is found.

79
00:04:49,306 --> 00:04:51,101
But notice what is not lost.

80
00:04:51,181 --> 00:04:54,403
The person still wakes.
Still keeps promises.

81
00:04:54,483 --> 00:04:57,111
Still meets the fruit
of what they have done.

82
00:04:57,926 --> 00:05:00,808
One rule matters here more than any other.

83
00:05:00,888 --> 00:05:05,971
When the carrier is removed, put nothing
in its place. Not a subtler soul.

84
00:05:06,051 --> 00:05:08,159
Not a stream. Not an energy.

85
00:05:08,239 --> 00:05:10,129
Not even emptiness itself.

86
00:05:10,209 --> 00:05:13,621
Many attempts to explain
rebirth deny the soul,

87
00:05:13,701 --> 00:05:16,284
and then quietly install a replacement.

88
00:05:16,364 --> 00:05:19,862
The Middle Way catches each
replacement as it appears.

89
00:05:20,669 --> 00:05:23,659
It also helps to keep
three kinds of claim apart.

90
00:05:23,739 --> 00:05:26,975
The logic shows that rebirth
does not need a carrier.

91
00:05:27,055 --> 00:05:29,896
The tradition affirms
that rebirth happens,

92
00:05:29,976 --> 00:05:34,094
and holds that affirmation in the
ordinary way it holds everything.

93
00:05:34,174 --> 00:05:38,510
And whether a particular memory of a
past life is accurate is a question for

94
00:05:38,590 --> 00:05:39,790
evidence.

95
00:05:40,414 --> 00:05:42,590
The first does not prove the second.

96
00:05:42,670 --> 00:05:47,372
Removing a bad argument against something
is not the same as giving a good argument

97
00:05:47,452 --> 00:05:50,565
for it. Emptiness does not prove rebirth.

98
00:05:50,645 --> 00:05:54,197
It removes the one objection
that seemed to stand against it.

99
00:05:54,997 --> 00:05:58,368
Rebirth is not a later addition
to the Buddha's teaching.

100
00:05:58,448 --> 00:06:01,044
On the night of his
awakening, the texts say,

101
00:06:01,124 --> 00:06:05,066
he recollected his own
past lives, one, two,

102
00:06:05,146 --> 00:06:07,023
a hundred, a thousand.

103
00:06:07,103 --> 00:06:11,860
Then he saw beings dying and being
reborn according to their deeds.

104
00:06:11,940 --> 00:06:15,478
Then he knew the ending of the
defilements, and was freed.

105
00:06:16,289 --> 00:06:20,434
In none of these does he see a
self passing from life to life.

106
00:06:20,514 --> 00:06:25,910
He sees lives, and the dependence of
lives on deeds. A pattern of conditioning.

107
00:06:25,990 --> 00:06:27,246
Not a passenger.

108
00:06:28,066 --> 00:06:31,641
The clearest correction
came to a monk named Sāti.

109
00:06:31,721 --> 00:06:35,731
Sāti believed that it is this very
same consciousness that roams and

110
00:06:35,811 --> 00:06:39,590
transmigrates, not
another. He was not crude.

111
00:06:39,670 --> 00:06:41,342
He did not posit a soul.

112
00:06:41,422 --> 00:06:45,803
He posited consciousness, and he
was trying to explain rebirth.

113
00:06:46,622 --> 00:06:48,526
The Buddha rebuked him sharply.

114
00:06:48,606 --> 00:06:52,235
Consciousness, he said,
arises dependently.

115
00:06:52,315 --> 00:06:55,265
Without a condition,
there is no consciousness.

116
00:06:55,345 --> 00:06:57,629
A fire is named by what it burns.

117
00:06:57,709 --> 00:07:00,129
A fire on logs is a log fire.

118
00:07:00,209 --> 00:07:02,833
A fire on grass is a grass fire.

119
00:07:02,913 --> 00:07:08,132
In the same way, consciousness is named
by its condition. Eye consciousness.

120
00:07:08,212 --> 00:07:11,017
Ear consciousness. Mind consciousness.

121
00:07:11,837 --> 00:07:15,778
Consciousness is not one thing
moving from fuel to fuel.

122
00:07:15,858 --> 00:07:20,412
Ask which fire is the same fire that
moved from the logs to the grass,

123
00:07:20,492 --> 00:07:23,799
and you have already imagined
a fire apart from its fuel.

124
00:07:24,622 --> 00:07:29,705
So a modern reader who rejects rebirth
because there is no soul to be reborn is

125
00:07:29,785 --> 00:07:34,855
in an odd position. They agree with
Sāti about what rebirth would require.

126
00:07:34,935 --> 00:07:36,761
And they disagree with the Buddha.

127
00:07:37,559 --> 00:07:42,574
A naked ascetic named Kassapa once asked
the Buddha whether suffering is made by

128
00:07:42,654 --> 00:07:44,925
oneself or by another.

129
00:07:45,005 --> 00:07:46,677
The Buddha declined both.

130
00:07:46,757 --> 00:07:50,794
To say the one who acts is the
one who experiences the result,

131
00:07:50,874 --> 00:07:53,063
he said, is eternalism.

132
00:07:53,143 --> 00:07:57,506
To say one acts and another
experiences is annihilationism.

133
00:07:57,586 --> 00:08:02,959
Avoiding both, he taught by the middle:
the chain of conditions, link by link.

134
00:08:03,774 --> 00:08:07,798
This is not evasion. It is an
exact answer to a better question.

135
00:08:07,878 --> 00:08:09,673
Not, is it the same one?

136
00:08:09,753 --> 00:08:11,701
But, on what does this depend?

137
00:08:12,501 --> 00:08:16,891
Another wanderer asked what a being
depends on between laying down this body

138
00:08:16,971 --> 00:08:18,644
and taking up the next.

139
00:08:18,724 --> 00:08:20,913
The Buddha answered with an image.

140
00:08:20,993 --> 00:08:24,717
When a flame is tossed by the
wind and carried some distance,

141
00:08:24,797 --> 00:08:26,510
it is fueled by the wind.

142
00:08:26,590 --> 00:08:30,849
In the same way, a being between
lives is fueled by craving.

143
00:08:31,657 --> 00:08:35,286
Even in the gap, there is
dependence, not a carrier.

144
00:08:35,366 --> 00:08:37,772
And what keeps the round turning is named.

145
00:08:37,852 --> 00:08:42,025
Not a self that wishes to
survive, but the thirst for being.

146
00:08:42,105 --> 00:08:45,707
That is why the ending of
craving is the ending of rebirth,

147
00:08:45,787 --> 00:08:48,184
and why that ending destroys no one.

148
00:08:49,002 --> 00:08:51,925
The Buddha also left some
questions unanswered.

149
00:08:52,005 --> 00:08:54,384
Does an awakened one exist after death?

150
00:08:54,464 --> 00:08:56,042
He turned the question back.

151
00:08:56,122 --> 00:08:58,963
If a fire went out in
front of you, he asked,

152
00:08:59,043 --> 00:09:00,621
which direction did it go?

153
00:09:00,701 --> 00:09:03,148
East, west, north, south?

154
00:09:03,228 --> 00:09:04,901
The question does not apply.

155
00:09:04,981 --> 00:09:09,144
It burned on its fuel, and when
the fuel ran out, it went out.

156
00:09:09,945 --> 00:09:12,079
The ending of rebirth is like that.

157
00:09:12,159 --> 00:09:15,888
Not the annihilation of a self,
but the ending of the fuel.

158
00:09:16,693 --> 00:09:20,186
The early teaching left a problem
for the schools that followed.

159
00:09:20,266 --> 00:09:23,596
An intention arises
and passes in a moment.

160
00:09:23,676 --> 00:09:26,807
Its fruit may come lives
later. What connects them?

161
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:29,656
The schools gave many answers.

162
00:09:29,736 --> 00:09:34,235
One said there is a person who is
neither the same as body and mind,

163
00:09:34,315 --> 00:09:38,447
nor different from them. Another
said the past deed still exists.

164
00:09:38,527 --> 00:09:42,510
Another said each deed plants
a seed in the mental stream.

165
00:09:42,590 --> 00:09:47,020
Another described a storehouse
consciousness that holds every seed until

166
00:09:47,100 --> 00:09:48,216
it ripens.

167
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:53,270
The Theravāda said the last moment of
one life is followed at once by a linking

168
00:09:53,350 --> 00:09:57,523
consciousness in the next, which
does not come over from the past,

169
00:09:57,603 --> 00:10:00,933
but arises in dependence
on it, like an echo,

170
00:10:01,013 --> 00:10:02,799
or the impression of a seal.

171
00:10:03,621 --> 00:10:08,165
Each bridge names something. Taken
as a thing with a nature of its own,

172
00:10:08,254 --> 00:10:10,810
each becomes a soul by another name.

173
00:10:10,890 --> 00:10:14,913
Taken as a way of speaking about
the dependence, each is harmless.

174
00:10:14,993 --> 00:10:17,934
The echo, especially, is exact.

175
00:10:18,745 --> 00:10:21,735
Nāgārjuna asked a more radical question.

176
00:10:21,815 --> 00:10:23,588
Is any bridge needed at all?

177
00:10:24,389 --> 00:10:29,200
If an action had a nature of its own,
he argued, it would be permanent.

178
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:31,890
A permanent action could
never have been done.

179
00:10:31,970 --> 00:10:35,124
And it would ripen again
and again, without end.

180
00:10:35,204 --> 00:10:40,278
A karma that existed by itself could
not do the work karma is supposed to do.

181
00:10:41,097 --> 00:10:45,025
So the agent, the action
and the fruit are all empty,

182
00:10:45,105 --> 00:10:47,403
and this is exactly why they work.

183
00:10:47,483 --> 00:10:51,438
The link between deed and
fruit is real and reliable,

184
00:10:51,518 --> 00:10:54,753
as the link between a rice
seed and rice is real.

185
00:10:54,833 --> 00:10:58,490
But it is not carried by something
traveling through the moments.

186
00:10:58,570 --> 00:11:03,096
The gap the bridges were built to span
is a gap only for things with a nature of

187
00:11:03,176 --> 00:11:04,376
their own.

188
00:11:04,885 --> 00:11:08,541
Nāgārjuna compares karma
to a magician's creation.

189
00:11:08,621 --> 00:11:14,044
A magician conjures a person, and that
person conjures another. They really act.

190
00:11:14,124 --> 00:11:17,712
A mirage is seen, and
travelers turn toward it.

191
00:11:17,792 --> 00:11:21,589
A dream can make the dreamer
weep. Karma is like this.

192
00:11:21,719 --> 00:11:25,393
Fully working, and nowhere
found standing by itself.

193
00:11:26,214 --> 00:11:29,028
He also looked at the
very moment of rebirth.

194
00:11:29,108 --> 00:11:32,439
If the last moment of one
life had already ceased,

195
00:11:32,519 --> 00:11:34,735
nothing would connect it to the next.

196
00:11:34,815 --> 00:11:38,335
If it had not ceased, two
lives would run at once.

197
00:11:38,415 --> 00:11:40,319
No link is found at the joint.

198
00:11:40,399 --> 00:11:42,724
The continuity is not denied.

199
00:11:42,804 --> 00:11:45,840
It is simply not found
as a thing that flows.

200
00:11:46,653 --> 00:11:49,861
Later, Candrakīrti drew the conclusion.

201
00:11:49,941 --> 00:11:51,613
No storehouse is needed.

202
00:11:51,693 --> 00:11:56,396
A deed that never existed by itself
never ceased by itself either.

203
00:11:56,476 --> 00:11:59,874
Its fruit can arise from
it, even long after,

204
00:11:59,954 --> 00:12:01,641
with nothing to keep it in.

205
00:12:01,721 --> 00:12:06,586
Tsongkhapa added that the very ceasing
of an action is itself a condition.

206
00:12:06,666 --> 00:12:09,630
And the person who is
reborn is the mere I:

207
00:12:09,710 --> 00:12:13,054
the I designated on
changing body and mind.

208
00:12:13,134 --> 00:12:14,847
Not found when looked for.

209
00:12:14,927 --> 00:12:18,556
And yet acting, remembering,
keeping promises,

210
00:12:18,636 --> 00:12:21,183
and meeting the results
of what it has done.

211
00:12:21,985 --> 00:12:27,095
Tibetan Buddhism describes the interval
between death and rebirth in detail.

212
00:12:27,175 --> 00:12:29,704
It is called the bardo, the in-between.

213
00:12:29,784 --> 00:12:34,133
As a person dies, the elements
dissolve one into another,

214
00:12:34,213 --> 00:12:38,050
until what the texts call the
clear light of death dawns.

215
00:12:38,861 --> 00:12:41,838
This clear light can be read in two ways.

216
00:12:41,918 --> 00:12:46,756
On one reading, it is a luminous
awareness beneath all experience,

217
00:12:46,836 --> 00:12:48,441
uncovered at death.

218
00:12:48,521 --> 00:12:50,493
That would be the traveler at last.

219
00:12:50,573 --> 00:12:55,194
On the reading these books follow,
luminosity is the knowing clarity of

220
00:12:55,274 --> 00:12:56,851
appearing itself.

221
00:12:56,931 --> 00:13:01,580
It is not a light behind things, and
it is empty like everything else.

222
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:04,677
What dawns at death is
not a hidden ground,

223
00:13:04,757 --> 00:13:07,576
but appearing recognized as unfixed.

224
00:13:08,398 --> 00:13:13,101
That is why the Tibetan teachers say the
best preparation for death is practice in

225
00:13:13,181 --> 00:13:16,185
life. Every moment is in between.

226
00:13:16,265 --> 00:13:21,611
If appearing is recognized as it is now,
there is nothing new to learn at death.

227
00:13:22,442 --> 00:13:27,593
Some teachers speak of a very subtle
mind that continues from life to life.

228
00:13:27,673 --> 00:13:31,085
Here the danger returns
in its most refined form.

229
00:13:31,165 --> 00:13:35,324
Read as a thing with its own
nature, it is Sāti's view again.

230
00:13:35,404 --> 00:13:40,908
Read as one more empty, changing
condition on which a person is designated,

231
00:13:40,988 --> 00:13:44,033
it is no more a carrier
than the ordinary mind.

232
00:13:44,113 --> 00:13:47,000
The step from one reading
to the other is short.

233
00:13:47,801 --> 00:13:52,979
In Japan, the Zen master Dōgen rejected
the view that the body perishes while a

234
00:13:53,059 --> 00:13:58,713
true self lives on and moves elsewhere,
like someone leaving a burning house.

235
00:13:58,793 --> 00:14:02,059
That, he said, is not
the Buddha's teaching.

236
00:14:02,890 --> 00:14:05,627
His best known image is firewood and ash.

237
00:14:05,716 --> 00:14:07,403
Firewood becomes ash.

238
00:14:07,483 --> 00:14:11,750
Yet we should not see the ash as
after and the firewood as before.

239
00:14:11,830 --> 00:14:14,318
Each abides fully in its own position.

240
00:14:14,398 --> 00:14:18,576
Life does not become death, as
winter does not become spring.

241
00:14:19,393 --> 00:14:21,487
This does not deny continuity.

242
00:14:21,567 --> 00:14:25,603
It denies that one thing passes
from the firewood into the ash.

243
00:14:25,683 --> 00:14:29,861
Each moment is complete, and needs
no substance running through it.

244
00:14:30,690 --> 00:14:33,559
There is also the story of Baizhang's fox.

245
00:14:33,639 --> 00:14:37,716
An old man told Baizhang that
long ago he had been an abbot.

246
00:14:37,796 --> 00:14:42,580
A student asked him whether a person of
great practice still falls into cause and

247
00:14:42,660 --> 00:14:47,023
effect. He answered: does not
fall into cause and effect.

248
00:14:47,103 --> 00:14:51,185
For that answer he was reborn
as a fox for five hundred lives.

249
00:14:52,006 --> 00:14:54,127
He asked Baizhang the same question.

250
00:14:54,207 --> 00:14:57,755
Baizhang answered: does not
obscure cause and effect.

251
00:14:57,835 --> 00:15:00,721
At these words, the old man was freed.

252
00:15:01,525 --> 00:15:06,920
Not falling into cause and effect treats
freedom as an escape from conditions.

253
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:11,105
Not obscuring cause and effect
is freedom as clarity about them.

254
00:15:11,185 --> 00:15:13,836
Emptiness gives no exemption from karma.

255
00:15:13,916 --> 00:15:17,590
Because nothing has a nature
of its own, karma works.

256
00:15:18,387 --> 00:15:20,807
A modern listener may still object.

257
00:15:20,887 --> 00:15:22,628
The mind depends on the brain.

258
00:15:22,708 --> 00:15:25,553
When the brain dies, the mind stops.

259
00:15:26,386 --> 00:15:29,608
The tradition agrees that
the mind depends on the body.

260
00:15:29,688 --> 00:15:34,785
But the objection usually assumes that
rebirth needs a mind that floats free and

261
00:15:34,865 --> 00:15:36,605
moves to another body.

262
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:39,608
That is exactly the
carrier the Buddha refused.

263
00:15:39,688 --> 00:15:42,448
And the objection has
a substance of its own.

264
00:15:42,528 --> 00:15:45,654
It takes matter as the one
thing that is really real.

265
00:15:45,734 --> 00:15:47,760
The Middle Way does not grant that either.

266
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:49,757
None of this proves rebirth.

267
00:15:49,837 --> 00:15:53,521
It shows only that the usual argument
against it depends on a picture the

268
00:15:53,601 --> 00:15:55,332
tradition never held.

269
00:15:56,137 --> 00:16:00,160
What about memory? Most people
remember nothing of a past life.

270
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:04,155
But memory was never the
carrier, even within one life.

271
00:16:04,235 --> 00:16:07,402
You remember almost nothing
of your first three years,

272
00:16:07,482 --> 00:16:09,222
and nothing of deep sleep.

273
00:16:09,302 --> 00:16:11,614
Yet you are held to the promises you made.

274
00:16:11,694 --> 00:16:16,165
What makes a later person continuous
with an earlier one is dependence,

275
00:16:16,245 --> 00:16:20,151
not a stored memory. Neither
the same, nor another.

276
00:16:20,957 --> 00:16:25,211
Is karma unfair, if the one who
suffers is not the one who acted?

277
00:16:25,291 --> 00:16:28,499
Karma is not a court, and
no one administers it.

278
00:16:28,579 --> 00:16:32,344
It describes how intention
tends to shape what follows.

279
00:16:32,424 --> 00:16:35,985
Not everything that happens
is the fruit of past action.

280
00:16:36,065 --> 00:16:38,580
And to look at a
suffering child and think,

281
00:16:38,661 --> 00:16:41,923
this is deserved, is
to misuse the teaching.

282
00:16:42,003 --> 00:16:45,243
It was given to free
beings, not to judge them.

283
00:16:46,065 --> 00:16:47,262
Is there evidence?

284
00:16:47,342 --> 00:16:52,289
Researchers such as Ian Stevenson and Jim
Tucker have studied young children who

285
00:16:52,369 --> 00:16:55,074
report memories of a previous life.

286
00:16:55,154 --> 00:16:57,547
Critics have raised serious questions.

287
00:16:57,627 --> 00:17:01,447
The view does not need to settle
the debate. But notice this.

288
00:17:01,527 --> 00:17:05,333
Even an accurate memory would
not show that a soul traveled.

289
00:17:05,413 --> 00:17:08,036
It would show a dependence
between two lives.

290
00:17:08,116 --> 00:17:10,745
It would fit the lamp, not the passenger.

291
00:17:11,557 --> 00:17:15,489
So what does this change for the
living, the dying and the grieving?

292
00:17:16,329 --> 00:17:22,024
For the living, the place where karma
is made is now. This act. This word.

293
00:17:22,104 --> 00:17:26,834
This turn of mind. Responsibility
does not weaken without a self.

294
00:17:26,914 --> 00:17:30,624
The mere I acts, and the
mere I meets the result.

295
00:17:30,704 --> 00:17:35,411
What falls away is only the anxious
sense of a ledger held against a self.

296
00:17:36,277 --> 00:17:39,526
For the dying, the view removes one dread:

297
00:17:39,606 --> 00:17:43,534
the image of an experience
held, a holder taken away,

298
00:17:43,614 --> 00:17:45,708
a holding left unfinished.

299
00:17:45,788 --> 00:17:50,043
It does not remove the fear of
pain, which can be met with care.

300
00:17:50,123 --> 00:17:53,602
It does not promise that the
person goes on as the same one.

301
00:17:53,682 --> 00:17:58,688
What it affirms, with the tradition,
is continuity without a carrier.

302
00:17:59,524 --> 00:18:02,596
For the grieving, grief is not a mistake.

303
00:18:02,676 --> 00:18:06,142
Love is real, and its
ending is a real loss.

304
00:18:06,222 --> 00:18:08,873
But the view removes two extra weights.

305
00:18:08,953 --> 00:18:12,297
The dead were not wiped
out, with nothing following.

306
00:18:12,377 --> 00:18:16,292
And they were not carried away,
to be found again as they were.

307
00:18:16,372 --> 00:18:18,479
Between the two is the lamp.

308
00:18:18,559 --> 00:18:22,777
A flame that was real, that has
gone out, and that lit others.

309
00:18:23,597 --> 00:18:27,172
And the end of rebirth? It is
not the destruction of someone.

310
00:18:27,252 --> 00:18:29,644
It is the fire that went in no direction.

311
00:18:29,724 --> 00:18:34,631
What ends is the fuel, the craving and
grasping on which the burning depended.

312
00:18:34,711 --> 00:18:37,036
Nirvāṇa is not another place.

313
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:40,097
It is this same appearing,
with the fixing ended.

314
00:18:40,918 --> 00:18:45,376
The round turns on not-knowing:
taking what is dependent as fixed.

315
00:18:45,456 --> 00:18:49,534
It ends with knowing: seeing that
what appears was never fixed.

316
00:18:49,614 --> 00:18:52,278
That seeing does not
wait for another life.

317
00:18:52,358 --> 00:18:55,499
The whole chain can be
seen in a single afternoon.

318
00:18:55,579 --> 00:18:57,568
And it can be seen through in one.

319
00:18:58,394 --> 00:19:00,814
This is all the continuity there is.

320
00:19:00,894 --> 00:19:02,662
The child becomes the adult.

321
00:19:02,742 --> 00:19:05,733
The one who sleeps
becomes the one who wakes.

322
00:19:05,813 --> 00:19:07,703
The deed becomes its fruit.

323
00:19:07,783 --> 00:19:10,724
One life becomes the
condition of the next.

324
00:19:11,537 --> 00:19:14,731
It needs no traveler. It
leaves no one cut off.

325
00:19:14,811 --> 00:19:18,472
One flame lights another,
and the lamp is burning now.

